{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/fiedlervector(normalized:tolerance:maxiterations:)"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Fiedler vector: λ₂ and a unit eigenvector of it, with the canonical sign (see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FiedlerVector"},{"type":"text","text":"); nil when the graph is not connected."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/fiedlerVector(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"fiedlerVector(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)","remoteSource":{"fileName":"FiedlerVector.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector.swift#L195"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fiedlerVector","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","text":"NoConvergence"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory13FiedlerVectorV","text":"FiedlerVector"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}],"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpectralGraphTheory"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE13fiedlerVector10normalized9tolerance13maxIterationsAD07FiedlerF0VyxGSgSb_SdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fiedlerVector"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":" = false, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-8, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"FiedlerVector","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory13FiedlerVectorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"normalized","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepted when its residual is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s (34 n from 5,000","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solver.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At least two vertices, "},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","style":"note"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"text":" when the Lanczos run on L⁺ spends ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":" matrix–vector","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"products (1,000 when nil) without converging, with the products spent and the Ritz","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"residual relative to 1\/λ₂. The run on σI − L that may come first hands over to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 + 20√n products or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whichever is smaller. Each shift-invert product is a conjugate-gradient solve that throws,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with its own iterations and relative residual, after 20,000 + 2n. Below 64 vertices the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dense solver answers and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":" is unused. Only a tolerance below rounding has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached the default limits in the measurements.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Throws","type":"aside","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"title":"GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/NoConvergence":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NoConvergence"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NoConvergence"}],"title":"NoConvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","abstract":[{"text":"The error an iterative method throws when it uses up its iteration limit without meeting its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stopping rule.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/noconvergence","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/FiedlerVector":{"type":"topic","title":"FiedlerVector","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FiedlerVector"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FiedlerVector"}],"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/fiedlervector","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Fiedler vector of a connected graph: a unit eigenvector of λ₂, the algebraic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connectivity, of the Laplacian (or of the normalized Laplacian), with one entry per vertex."}]},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory":{"title":"SpectralGraphTheory","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph/fiedlerVector(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)":{"title":"fiedlerVector(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/fiedlervector(normalized:tolerance:maxiterations:)","abstract":[{"text":"The Fiedler vector: λ₂ and a unit eigenvector of it, with the canonical sign (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"FiedlerVector","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); nil when the graph is not connected.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/fiedlerVector(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fiedlerVector","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FiedlerVector","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory13FiedlerVectorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"}}}